/* Export: PalSpriteSetRenderMode. Borrows writable sprite; null returns 0/error6, success1/error0. Stores complete mode word without validation. Legacy D3D dispatcher recognizes1..4; newer recognizes1..11. Legacy draw restores default blend after non1 modes; unknown inputs therefore use initialized default state. Newer11 disables blending and selects texture RGB; normal render walk does not restore those two states, whereas TargetRenderListDraw restores defaults before each callback. Portable draw commands carry blend_disabled and texture_rgb independently of the unchanged mode word. The ordinary priority-sorted engine walk preserves those states across frames; the target-walk state helper resets before every callback and after the list. CPU, wgpu, Switch deko3d and Vita GXM consume the resolved flags. Native DIB and D3D kernels are distinct; portable software uses recovered D3D RGB equations. See per-build callback/draw/blend evidence under reverse/evidence/pal-graphics. */
