/* Export: PalChannelCopyEx. Borrows two sprite pointers and a required readable 16-byte RECT for the call; the first sprite is writable. Null sprites, channels outside 0..3, empty clipped overlap, lock failure or operation outside 0..2 return 0; successful traversal returns 1. RECT null is not checked natively. Channel indices address native BGRA bytes and are mapped explicitly to portable RGBA. Operations are copy, saturated addition and rounded product (257*(destination*source+128))>>16. Clips the destination rectangle then offsets/clips source coordinates. A pointer-identical sprite is locked/unlocked once, and traversal is top-to-bottom/left-to-right with immediate writes, preserving overlapping alias feedback. The portable arena adapter rejects invalid handles and impossible physical dimensions; it models byte operations but does not reproduce driver lock failures or native last-error residue. */
