/* Export: PalWait. Creates a wait task with four-byte work storage and returns the owned scheduler task pointer or null. First scheduled callback installs the countdown callback. Each later tick leaves -1 unchanged; otherwise decrements with wrapping arithmetic and frees the task when the result reaches zero. Input 0 becomes -1 and consequently waits indefinitely. This function queues a wait; it does not block the calling OS thread. Native task/work pointers are borrowed for access and scheduler-owned until deferred release; null task selects current task except GetTaskData, where it selects the separately chosen data context. Null with no context is guarded by the portable adapter, unlike native unchecked dereferences. Portable generation handles are not ABI pointer words. Work size is 4 bytes; task flags 0x10001 select blocking insertion after current task. */
